class: abi
profiles: standard
summary: platform/linux's epoll and signalfd numbers, struct epoll_event, packed on x86-64 alone, and struct signalfd_siginfo, and a signal's bit in the kernel's mask; platform/kqueue's filters, flags, timer units and struct kevent on Darwin and FreeBSD; and platform/libc's sigprocmask operations, signals, O_NONBLOCK, F_GETFL and SOCK_NONBLOCK where it exists, each held to the system's own C headers, with each record read from C as C filled it and filled for C to read
